  "notes": "Kinto Gmail Notification Workflow (v3 - Task Events - Hardcoded Fixed for n8n Free Tier)\n\n**VERSION 3 HARDCODED FIXED UPDATES:**\nAll environment variables replaced with hardcoded values.\nBoth structural bugs fixed:\n\n**BUG FIX 1 — Switch Node Router:**\nReplaced n8n-nodes-base.if (2 outputs) with n8n-nodes-base.switch (3 outputs):\n- Output 0: eventType === \"task.created\"\n- Output 1: eventType === \"task.assigned\"\n- Output 2: eventType === \"task.updated\" AND newStatus === \"completed\"\n\n**BUG FIX 2 — Data Context Preservation:**\nExtract Payload node now stores original webhook data.\nAll filter nodes reference original payload using $('Extract Payload').item.json.*\nEmail nodes receive taskTitle, priority, timestamp from original payload.\n\n**HARDCODED VALUES:**\n- API URL: https://3000-ibzoxkm20wtqn19ljztzp-68f29bbc.us2.manus.computer/api/trpc/users.getByRoleWithApiKey\n- API Key: 71fbd697bba9d0a9d90e14178fafd39c674dd36cc66edddc69994b73348ae834\n- Auth Header: x-api-key\n- Sender Email: optimizedhubllc@gmail.com\n\n**KEY FEATURES:**\n- Plain text emails (not HTML) for accessibility\n- Compliance footer on all emails\n- Role-based recipient filtering\n- Separate branches for each event type\n- Uses API key authentication (x-api-key header)\n- No environment variables required\n- Proper data context preservation\n\n**EVENT ROUTING (Switch Node):**\n1. Webhook Trigger receives event from Kinto EventBus\n2. Extract Payload parses event fields and stores original data\n3. Event Router (Switch) branches to specific event handlers:\n   - Output 0: task.created → Get assigned user → Send notification\n   - Output 1: task.assigned → Get assigned user → Send notification\n   - Output 2: task.updated (completed) → Get all users → Send broadcast\n\n**DATA FLOW:**\n1. Webhook receives payload\n2. Extract Payload stores: eventType, taskId, taskTitle, timestamp, hubId, priority, assignedTo, oldStatus, newStatus\n3. Switch routes based on eventType + newStatus\n4. HTTP Request fetches users from API\n5. Filter nodes combine API response with original payload data\n6. Email nodes reference taskTitle, priority, timestamp from filter nodes\n\n**WEBHOOK PAYLOAD FORMAT (v3):**\n{\n  \"hub_id\": \"uuid\",\n  \"event_type\": \"task.created|task.assigned|task.updated\",\n  \"task_id\": \"uuid\",\n  \"task_title\": \"string\",\n  \"assigned_to\": \"number (user ID) | null\",\n  \"priority\": \"low|medium|high\",\n  \"old_status\": \"pending|in_progress|completed\" (only for task.updated),\n  \"new_status\": \"pending|in_progress|completed\" (only for task.updated),\n  \"timestamp\": \"ISO 8601 datetime\"\n}\n\n**SETUP INSTRUCTIONS (n8n Free Tier):**\n1. Copy this workflow JSON\n2. Import into n8n cloud\n3. Replace 'YOUR_LLC_GMAIL_CREDENTIAL_ID' with your actual Gmail credential ID\n4. No environment variables needed - all values are hardcoded\n5. Test with sample task events\n6. Activate the workflow\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES:**\n- Update the API URL if the Kinto dev server URL changes\n- Update the API key if a new one is generated\n- Sender email is optimizedhubllc@gmail.com\n- All other workflow logic remains unchanged from v3\n\n**MIGRATION FROM V3 (Environment Variables):**\nV3 used environment variable placeholders and If nodes.\nThis fixed version (v3-hardcoded-fixed) uses:\n- Hardcoded values\n- Switch node for proper 3-way routing\n- Data context preservation via $('Extract Payload').item.json.*\n\nReady for n8n free tier import without any configuration.\n\n**DOCUMENTATION:**\nSee TASK_WEBHOOK_PAYLOADS.md for complete payload documentation.\nSee API_KEY_N8N_SETUP.md for API key setup guide.\n\n**COMPLIANCE:**\nAll emails include footer: \"Kinto Care is a logistics and data coordination tool. No medical diagnosis provided.\""
